  "notes": "The roofless ruin of a honey-stone abbey church 44 m by 16 m, its east gable standing 14 m round an empty pointed window, the nave walls broken to 1.5-9 m over the stumps of two rows of round piers (one fallen across the nave), and on the south (local -X) the grassed footings of a 24 m cloister with four arches still standing. Front (the west door) faces local -Z; carves nothing.",
